{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":464031,"name":"Tyler Harden","username":"durden","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/durden/{size}/111800_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-12T15:16:20.729Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-464031-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-464031-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSomewhere else…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-464031-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-464031-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUser has Settings → Agent → Execution on Local Computer → Always allow. Persisted setting on the box confirms localToolPermission: “always” with no localToolPermissionCeiling. Repeated ExternalShell calls still fail immediately with the canned UNAPPROVED message. No approval card appears in the UI. Same failure class was also seen from another agent’s subagent (Chief of Staff / LinkedIn resume probe) on the same account today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-464031-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-464031-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnsure Execution on Local Computer = Always allow (user reports UI shows this; box settings file matches).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFrom agent Aristotle, invoke ExternalShell with a trivial command, e.g. echo probe \u0026amp;\u0026amp; whoami \u0026amp;\u0026amp; hostname.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve immediate failure with the UNAPPROVED text above.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve no local-computer approval card.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-464031-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-464031-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI was prompted to permit Grok Bot agents to run local commands and clicked always allow. Confirmed this in settings. I would like that setting to be honored so they can run commands locally on my machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-464031-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-464031-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/1/c/1c0bb328a283f689d941980dd074c0d4c0a6c317.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/406r1PQEdDkpSdkyqsBbw0Mizn9.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"grok bot external shell issue.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/c/1c0bb328a283f689d941980dd074c0d4c0a6c317_2_474x500.jpeg\" alt=\"grok bot external shell issue.jpg\" data-base62-sha1=\"406r1PQEdDkpSdkyqsBbw0Mizn9\" width=\"474\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/c/1c0bb328a283f689d941980dd074c0d4c0a6c317_2_474x500.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/c/1c0bb328a283f689d941980dd074c0d4c0a6c317_2_711x750.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/1/c/1c0bb328a283f689d941980dd074c0d4c0a6c317_2_948x1000.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"EAEAEA\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003egrok bot external shell issue.jpg\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1614×1700 410 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u0