el=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-13T08:38:20.946Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":96,"reads":9,"readers_count":8,"score":491.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":168180,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-externalshell-blocked-despite-always-allow","display_username":"Tyler Harden","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-local-exec-daemon-on-macos-dies-after-staying-healthy-mac-unreachable-until-leftover-processes-are-killed/168548","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Grok Bot local-exec-daemon on macOS dies after staying healthy; Mac unreachable until leftover processes are killed","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/grok-bot-local-exec-flaps-between-windows-and-mac-when-both-desktop-apps-are-open/168583","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Grok Bot local-exec flaps between Windows and Mac when both desktop apps are open","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":122284,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-externalshell-blocked-despite-always-allow/168180/1","reactions":[{"id":"heavy_plus_sign","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":464709,"name":"Mohit","username":"mohitjain","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png","created_at":"2026-08-13T08:35:08.633Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey! Thanks for the detailed report. Your Always allow setting is genuinely set, so this isn’t something you misconfigured - it’s an issue we’re tracking. To unblock you now:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quit Grok Bot with Cmd+Q (closing the window isn’t enough).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Terminal, run \u003ccode\u003eps aux | grep local-exec-daemon\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003ekill\u003c/code\u003e any leftover processes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRelaunch Grok Bot.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Settings → Agent → Execution on Local Computer, switch to Ask every time, then back to Always allow.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdating alone won’t clear this, so run the steps even on the newest build. Let me know if \u003ccode\u003eExternalShell\u003c/code\u003e still errors afterward.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-13T08:35:08.633Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":16.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":168180,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-externalshell-blocked-despite-always-allow","display_username":"Mohit","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":103596,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-externalshell-blocked-despite-always-allow/168180/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":470433,"name":"Artemis","username":"Artemis1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/ecccb3/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:29:59.025Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eSame issue here on Mac + Grok Bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen an agent tries ExternalShell (open Chrome, Finder, or \u003ca href=\"http://youtube.com/feed/history\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eyoutube.com/feed/history\u003c/a\u003e), it fails immediately with: “That action was not approved on the user’s computer… set Settings → Agent → Execution on Local Computer to Always allow.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo Allow card appears in the Grok Bot chat. I have looked for it and I cannot find it. I also cannot find that exact setting anymore. In Cursor it now looks like Settings → Agents → Approvals \u0026amp; Execution, not “Execution on Local Computer / Always allow.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes a later “try again” works. Most of the time it stays blocked and I never see a prompt. I was also offline when one of these requests happened, and still saw no card when I came back.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the same “no approval card” failure, plus the setting name/path seems to have changed, so I don’t know what to toggle.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":8,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-08-20T18:29:59.025Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":2,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":11.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":168180,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-externalshell-blocked-despite-always-allow","display_username":"Artemis","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"f